{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797958-how-prevalent-are-conspiracies-on-their-home-turf","id":797958,"title":"How prevalent are Conspiracies on their home turf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-01T13:54:32-08:00","id":797958,"title":"How prevalent are Conspiracies on their home turf?","content":"I don\u2019t know if this particular topic is addressed somewhere in the line (I only have read the core and Compacts And Conspiracies).<br /> <br /> Some Conspiracies (and, I guess, Compacts) have a canon HQ where their head honcho resides and does whatever the heads of a conspiracies like to do. But just how much of a presence the members of the conspiracies have in that particular city and how is nightlife different because of that?<br /> <br /> I am asking this because the two biggest cities in my country (I\u2019m Italian, so Rome and Milan) are both the headquarters of conspiracies, and those whose highest members are fairly important for the organization itself (take the Lucifuge out of the Lucifuge and you have\u2026 a great plot line, but a completely different set of hunters. Baudolino is slightly less important but still no one to laugh at). Also, they know each other and have tea parties. Ok, maybe not tea parties, but I like that image. I mean, if I go by crossover canon (and I like to go as much by canon as possible), this kinda limits what sort of stories I can tell.<br /> <br /> In my games the Malleus Maleficarum has a \u201cpact\u201d with the resident vampires (the Lancea takes blood tolls from the citizens and gives some of them directly to the Inquisition, Baudolino is happy, the MM looks the other way), and Vatican City is strictly off limits, but I think I am stretching canon as much as I personally can.<br /> And I don\u2019t know what the presence of the Lucifuge could do to Milan. I mean, she\u2019s an ancient badass, fairly protected and hell (eh eh) bent on destroying evil. Being supernatural in Milan must not be fun.<br /> <br /> Are there some info about this? I know I can bend canon and do what I want cause a pirate is free and I am a pirate, but having definite answers would help a lot. Thanks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:13:39-08:00","id":797970,"title":"","content":"Canonically there's no answer but I like to play it as though the Conspiracies are among the biggest baddest players in the entire WoD. So to me, the MM rule Rome with an iron fist. You might get the occasional witch or demon hiding beneath notice, but no monsters have a serious power base. (I don't think Baudolino would strike a pact with Rome's Vampires, it's too risky, he'd get blood from further away).<br /> <br /> Vatican City itself would be a fortress, covered in so many protective Benedicitions that the average vampire would run in Fear Frenzy before they even got close. And the reason the Pontifical Swiss Guard still have swords and halberds is so they can bless them with the Wrathful Sword of St. Michael.<br /> <br /> (I see Vatican City as the setting for a heist plot. The ultimate secure fortress that players might raid for rare manuscripts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:20:23-08:00","id":797975,"title":"","content":"Up until Blood and Smoke came out, I described the Mediterranean as a killbox, a place monsters avoided at all costs. Even with Vampire's Athens poking a hole in that and creating wiggle room, I still largely run the Mediterranean as a tough place to exist as a monster. I mean, in that region, you have the Malleus Maleficarum, The Lucifigue, the Aegis Kai Doru, and the Ascending Ones all claiming major territory there, with the Knights of Saint George having their former power base in Britain not that far away, and certainly with Cheiron probably also keeping up lodgings.<br /> <br /> That power can concentrate in other areas, sure, but as it stands, the Mediterranean is <i>not</i> a nice place to be as a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:40:24-08:00","id":797985,"title":"","content":"I tend to give Conspiracies less political and geographical power, in exchange for more efficacy. Gangs and mafias that hold a city with an iron grip tend to have problems with secrecy, because an important part of intimidation is knowing who is intimidating you and what they're capable of. I tend to run Hunter groups as extremely efficient and deadly, to give them the weight they need to keep the supernatural at bay. My Hunter groups move in the shadows and instil fear in the supernatural precisely by being unknown. Vampires exist in Rome (especially the Lancea), but they live in fear that the random guy they drag into an alley to feed off ends up being a Hunter who knows powerful Benedictions. So they are far more cautious and sneaky than vampires in other places.<br /> <br /> My supernatural vs. Hunter headcanon is a cold war in the shadows. The sides of the conflict don't fight in the open, they try to outmanoeuvre each other with secrecy, assassination, pawns and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:51:34-08:00","id":797990,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what I mean with &quot;this limits the stories I can tell&quot;. I have to juggle this hotpot of conspiracies <i>and </i>Vampire 2e pictured Rome as one of the Lancea strongholds*. And even then, I had to tone that down a bit because the Romans are <i>seriously</i> not as religious as it may seem from the outside, and a Catholic may not like the teachings of Longinus.<br /> <br /> I also have the habit of toning up how much corruption, chaos and mismanagement there is in every Italian organization, Church included. Stuff like, for as much as he'd like otherwise, Baudolino has only enough power to protect himself, the Pope and a bunch of other important cardinals (still, Vatican City is a &quot;rocks fall, eveyone dies&quot; zone for vampires, but it's a really small area to defend), the internal divide is quickly evolving in a civil war and secret documents are fairly easy to recover. Or, the Lucifuge has, like, less than ten people at her disposal and their only goal is her safety. In short words, conspiracies are fairly short on manpower, and their sandcastles may crumble at any minute.<br /> <br /> Still, the CofD is a toolbox and I like hearing what others think. Thanks!<br /> <br /> * In my write up the political set up is more complicated than that, without being directly contradicting. Basically the Lancea has lots of power and influence but doesn't nominally reign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T15:49:23-08:00","id":798005,"title":"","content":"VALKYRIE can likely reach damn near anywhere in the world, but I'm not sure how many dedicated office buildings and bases they have other than that one R&amp;D facility. I'd like to think they're sort of like X-COM in that regard, with one central bunker heading up their operations, and then strike teams all ready to deploy where they're needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T20:10:29-08:00","id":798073,"title":"","content":"In my own chronicles I have the Vigil in Washington DC covered by an alliance of Task Force Valkyrie and the Lucifuge. Most of their efforts are focused on preventing the representatives and apparatus of government from being too deeply suborned by the supernatural, which is a full time job even for two Conspiracies. As long as you don't make yourself a high profile target the big anglers are probably going to ignore you, or at least leave you for the more local cells to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T21:30:39-08:00","id":798095,"title":"","content":"Belial's Brood, specifically the faction known as the Mercy Seat, have their oldest and largest stronghold in Genoa, where they constantly chip away at the Catholic Church, avoiding direct confrontations. So there's something you could add to the vampire side of things.<br /> <br /> I've never really run a game that took place in one of Hunters' canon strongholds or headquarters. There was one with a Task Force Valkyrie barracks, though. They operated in a military base of some sort, it's been so long I forget which. It was mostly a jumping point where Valkyrie could jump off into the Caribbean if needed, but there were a group of hunters there, including one military prisoner. The entire operation was overseen by a bully of an officer who was a ghoul. The players shifted to the Abbey before that plot was resolved but they both died off-screen. Before Hunter came out I had cribbed some stuff from Hunter the Reckoning that led to having a very influential Hermit having retired to the city.<br /> <br /> What I'd factor in is this. Basically, providing they aren't completely inept, if a Hunter has five dots of Status, providing they live in a set place and aren't moving around, they've begun molding the world around them. Not necessarily in a magical sense, but these are people who have seen a lot of shit. They know not to trust certain kinds of people, they know some people might succumb too easily to promises of power. And through whatever means, they're going to try to make sure the right people get in the right places, as well as have people who will report back to them about oddities or just keep tabs on local news agencies. That's just regular hunters, though.<br /> <br /> When you're talking about conspiracies and their bases of operations you're talking about a place that's had multiple Status 5 and probably a lot more Status 2-4 there for decades or even centuries. I wouldn't go out and make an army of hunters, but they would have access to enough people that trust them that they could have a makeshift army, if necessary. Police, local gangs or tribes, militias and political activists, basically any organized and large group of people would have been watched and infiltrated or allied with, with at least a few people knowing what's really up and being willing to help if the situation comes up. And of course, in decades of preparation you've no doubt gathered enough ordinance to arm them.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say these places are completely supernatural free, though. Sure it's easy to weed out vampires if you have a large and organized force, but there's always going to be one paranoid loner or some elder in torpor who could easily be overlooked. And most monsters don't organize in neat factions where you can track one back to its den and eliminate it. There's a lot more than the gamelines in the World of Darkness, and for a lot of the more dangerous things there's nothing anyone could do about it. As horrible a time a mortal would have facing a second edition werewolf down, a mortal facing down an idigam would probably gladly switch with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T00:53:57-08:00","id":798154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797958-how-prevalent-are-conspiracies-on-their-home-turf?p=797975#post797975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even with Vampire's Athens poking a hole in that and creating wiggle room</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't take the sample cities as cannon in this regard. I don't think they were designed with crossover in mind. Compacts and Conspiracies says that the AKDs leaders have a personal Vigil over Athens and monsters there are <i>terrified </i>of them.<br /> <br /> Given this direct contradiction, I think it's up to us to decide for ourselves who's actually more likely to control Athens, the AKD or vampires. I'm betting on the AKD, once you start getting to True Fae Prop levels of stupid-power, which they explicitly have in Athens, it isn't too hard to powergame into being nigh unbeatable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T01:09:48-08:00","id":798157,"title":"","content":"well, considering that the AKD's interest in vampires is pretty low (their are neither part of the &quot;ancient treason&quot; nor having special interest/ability to make relics), I don't think both of them need to contradict each other- the vampires hold political power, the AKD present a power block against them, with some sort of &quot;cold peace&quot; going between he groups. Night Stalkers explicitly says that the AKD sees vampires as a &quot;minor threat&quot; compared to witches and werewolves, and that they even trade secrets and knowledge with each other. The relationships between the two is often complicated, especially that the vampires of Athene are not a united group and have a number of covenants working against each other. It is not far from possible that the AKD has an alliance with one group, a truce with another and work actively against the third while using (and being used) by the other covenants.<br /> <br /> Not, being a mage or a shifter in Athene- that should be an whole other story...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T04:16:35-08:00","id":798194,"title":"","content":"The bigger contradiction is that the Mysterium have an Athenaeum. They're so afraid fo the AKD that they use a public museum for their Mithraum?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the reason the Pontifical Swiss Guard still have swords and halberds is so they can bless them with the Wrathful Sword of St. Michael. </div> </div> </div>That's a really good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even then, I had to tone that down a bit because the Romans are <i>seriously</i> not as religious as it may seem from the outside, and a Catholic may not like the teachings of Longinus. </div> </div> </div>Most people from Rome haven't been turned into cannabalistic ghost monsters. Also, I don't think Rome would be a stronghold because it's people are highly religious, it's because the Lancea are at least partially based around protecting the mortal church. It's a priority for them as a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T05:45:26-08:00","id":798218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797958-how-prevalent-are-conspiracies-on-their-home-turf?p=798194#post798194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger contradiction is that the Mysterium have an Athenaeum. They're so afraid fo the AKD that they use a public museum for their Mithraum?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well... I imagine the Seers are also interested in stealing stuff from the Mysterium and the Mysterium is concerned with the Seers.<br /> <br /> So if they can use a public museum and still be concerned with the Seers, they can use a public museum and be concerned with the AKD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797958-how-prevalent-are-conspiracies-on-their-home-turf?p=798194#post798194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a really good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797958-how-prevalent-are-conspiracies-on-their-home-turf?p=797975#post797975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, in that region, you have the Malleus Maleficarum, The Lucifigue, the Aegis Kai Doru, and the Ascending Ones all claiming major territory there</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it's easy to overlook but the Canites formed in Italy too and probably have a <b>much </b>stronger presence in that region than in most places. Between the other Conspiracies in the area dividing the monsters attention; and the enormous political unrest to the south providing a place they can hide from mortal authorities (they look like terrorists to an outside observer after all) the Middle East is bound to have a large crop of Canites. If the Sources are physically on Earth, I'd bet they're in Italy too. The Canites, Lucifuge, and MM do have that connection.<br /> <br /> (Plus, whatever the British, French, Spanish and German governments have going for them. The USA founded 2 Conspiracies in under a century. European nations have been going strong for far longer and built empires at various points. They'd have cooked something up at some point in their history)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-02-2016, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T06:25:21-08:00","id":798226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well... I imagine the Seers are also interested in stealing stuff from the Mysterium and the Mysterium is concerned with the Seers.So if they can use a public museum and still be concerned with the Seers, they can use a public museum and be concerned with the AKD. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but as pointed out previously the AKD are really strong in Athens, whilst it's pretty standard practice for the Pentacle and Seers to simply ignore each other. Further, it's not just any public museum, it's the National Archaeological Museum; and they've got quite a few members in influencial positions within it. I'd assume the AKD would be watching such a place very carefully for relics.<br /> Also, the reason they use the museum is for their mystery cult centred on the Antikythera Mechanism. If the witches of Athens are so afraid of the AKD, they could just steal the thing and move somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T06:43:56-08:00","id":798230,"title":"","content":"Ah, now that's probably just the AKD not really being cannon in Mage. The books are directly contradicting each other here, so crossover storytellers have to decide for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T10:22:10-08:00","id":798308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797958-how-prevalent-are-conspiracies-on-their-home-turf?p=798154#post798154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't take the sample cities as cannon in this regard. I don't think they were designed with crossover in mind. Compacts and Conspiracies says that the AKDs leaders have a personal Vigil over Athens and monsters there are <i>terrified </i>of them.<br /> <br /> Given this direct contradiction, I think it's up to us to decide for ourselves who's actually more likely to control Athens, the AKD or vampires. I'm betting on the AKD, once you start getting to True Fae Prop levels of stupid-power, which they explicitly have in Athens, it isn't too hard to powergame into being nigh unbeatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>eh. Even if I did take that route, it did open the idea to me that it's more fun to e a struggle, even if Hunters control the table there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T14:50:43-08:00","id":798406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797958-how-prevalent-are-conspiracies-on-their-home-turf?p=798230#post798230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, now that's probably just the AKD not really being cannon in Mage. The books are directly contradicting each other here, so crossover storytellers have to decide for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I mentioned it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}